+### Native stateful GDN typed TensorIR builder
+
+The native recurrent GDN frontend is the first model operator on the typed
+builder path. HIR analysis freezes seven inputs in order: packed BF16 QKV,
+BF16 `a`, BF16 `b`, FP32 `A_log`, BF16 `dt_bias`, read-write FP32 state, and
+INT32/INT64 state indices. Gates and parameter vectors may use explicit
+zero-stride broadcast views; packed input, indices, and result remain dense,
+while state may have a row pitch no smaller than its payload.
+
+The bridge builds the stable-softplus recurrence with typed `SliceOp`,
+`ReshapeOp`, `ConvertOp`, pointwise ops, `ReduceOp`, `BroadcastOp`, `MatmulOp`,
+`GatherRowsOp`, `ScatterRowsOp`, `TransposeOp`, and `ConcatenateOp`. BF16
+`dt_bias` is explicitly converted to FP32 before `a + dt_bias`. The state update
+keeps the reviewed BF16 beta round-trip and the trailing-transpose alignment
+attribute. Identity broadcasts are elided because TensorIR forbids no-op
+`BroadcastOp`; the schedule producer correspondingly supplies tiles only for
+non-unit iteration-space dimensions. TensorIR verification runs before
+canonical printing or lowering; the compiler then consumes that exact
+in-memory module. The former per-head and batched handwritten GDN MLIR emitters
+are not retained as a fallback.
+
